<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Kalmar Union</h1><p class="st-meta">1397 CE – 1523 CE · capital Copenhagen</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Personal union of Denmark, Norway and Sweden under one monarch, created by Queen Margaret I in 1397 and broken by Sweden's secession in 1523.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margaret-i-of-denmark">Margaret I</a>, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-iv-of-denmark">Valdemar IV of Denmark</a> and widow of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haakon-vi-of-norway">Haakon VI of Norway</a>, became ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and, after defeating King Albert of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-mecklenburg">Mecklenburg</a> in 1389, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> too. In 1397 her great-nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-of-pomerania">Eric of Pomerania</a> was crowned king of all three realms at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar">Kalmar</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The union shared a monarch and foreign policy, but each kingdom kept its own laws, councils and nobility. Danish dominance and wars with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-holstein">Holstein</a> caused resentment in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/engelbrekt-engelbrektsson">Engelbrekt</a> rebellion of 1434 began a century of conflict. Swedish regents of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sture-family">Sture family</a> often ruled in practice.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-ii-of-denmark">Christian II</a> reconquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> in 1520 and executed some eighty nobles and clergy in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stockholm-bloodbath">Stockholm Bloodbath</a>, provoking a revolt led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustav-i-of-sweden">Gustav Vasa</a>, who was elected king of Sweden in 1523. The union ended, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> continued together as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/denmark-norway">Denmark-Norway</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kalmar-union.jpg" alt="Kalmar Union" width="320" height="298"><figcaption>Image: Ssolbergj · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kalmar_Union_ca._1400.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1397 CE – 1523 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Copenhagen</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Margaret I, Eric of Pomerania, Christian II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Danish, Swedish, Norwegian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/denmark">Denmark</a>, <a href="/countries/norway">Norway</a>, <a href="/countries/sweden">Sweden</a>, <a href="/countries/finland">Finland</a>, <a href="/countries/iceland">Iceland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Union of Kalmar, Kalmarunionen</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1460&amp;focus=kalmar-union" aria-label="Kalmar Union on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4954 279 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kalmar Union lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5274 535L5274 535M5274 535L5225 425M5274 535L5381 440M5274 535L5274 535"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5274 535h0M5225 425h0M5381 440h0M5274 535h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5274 535h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5274 535h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Copenhagen. <a href="/atlas?year=1460&amp;focus=kalmar-union">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
